### UniBite — Test: POST /api/listings/delete
### Run #1 first; the HTTP Client keeps the session cookie for the rest.

### 1) Login
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/auth/login.php
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "dimitris",
  "password": "unibite2025"
}

### 2) Delete listing #1 (expect success)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/listings/delete.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

listing_id=1

### 3) Delete #1 again (expect 409 Already deleted)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/listings/delete.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

listing_id=1

### 4) Delete a non-existent listing (expect 404 Listing not found)
POST http://localhost/unibite/api/listings/delete.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

listing_id=99999
